{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Good.</b> He said: what does a wise man have in walking his soul in the way of fools, whose soul is never filled? Enough for him is what is found, what is visible to the eye — even though what is visible and what arises in the soul's thought is vanity. Another interpretation: that it be better, 'the sight of the eyes' — matters of life, as in the verse: what advantage to its owner, if not seeing with his eyes."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:56.800815672Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}